(New Doctor Website + CMS Onboarding Steps) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Date: 2026-07-08) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Goal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This SOP helps you create a new doctor website using the same setup as Dr. Prashant and) Tj
T*
(manage it via CMS.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 1: Collect Intake Data) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Collect and verify the following:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Doctor full name, degree, specialty, years of experience) Tj
T*
(- Registration number, certifications, awards) Tj
T*
(- Clinic address, city, pincode, phone, WhatsApp, email) Tj
T*
(- Clinic timings \(weekdays, Saturday, Sunday\)) Tj
T*
(- About profile content) Tj
T*
(- Services list) Tj
T*
(- Expertise topics and detailed content) Tj
T*
(- Testimonials and FAQs) Tj
T*
(- SEO data \(meta title, meta description, keywords\)) Tj
T*
(- Domain and DNS access details) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 2: Create Doctor Bootstrap in Project) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Run this command from project root:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(npm run onboard:doctor -- --id <doctor-id> --name "Dr. Full Name" --username) Tj
T*
(<cms-username> --specialty "Specialty") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Example:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(npm run onboard:doctor -- --id amol --name "Dr. Amol Patil" --username amol --specialty) Tj
T*
("Cardiology") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This command does two things:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Creates config/<doctor-id>-profile.json) Tj
T*
(- Adds doctor entry in config/doctors-list.json) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 3: Fill New Doctor Config) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Open config/<doctor-id>-profile.json and replace all placeholders.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Mandatory checks:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Correct doctor and clinic details) Tj
T*
(- Correct images and contact fields) Tj
T*
(- services populated) Tj
ET
