T*
(Verify CMS backend and services:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- PM2 process healthy) Tj
T*
(- API routes reachable) Tj
T*
(- Nginx domain mapping correct) Tj
T*
(- SSL active and HTTP redirects to HTTPS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 8: Cache Bust After JS Changes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If frontend/CMS JS is updated, bump script version query so browser loads fresh file.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Example pattern:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(assets/js/app.js?v=20260708d) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 9: Go-Live Checklist) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Before final approval:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Desktop and mobile layout check) Tj
T*
(- Call, WhatsApp, contact form check) Tj
T*
(- SEO title and meta description check) Tj
T*
(- No console errors on key pages) Tj
T*
(- Doctor approval received) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step 10: Post Go-Live Monitoring \(24-48 Hours\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Check app and API logs) Tj
T*
(- Verify feedback submissions) Tj
T*
(- Check for 404 or broken links) Tj
T*
(- Keep backup of config and deployment notes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Important Operational Notes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Always verify correct running CMS path before editing on VPS.) Tj
T*
(- Preview issues usually come from token persistence, link propagation, or stale cache.) Tj
T*
(- Keep expertise_items and expertise synchronized to avoid Read More mismatch.) Tj
T*
(- Do not skip cache-busting when script changes are deployed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Quick One-Doctor Execution Flow) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Run onboarding command.) Tj
T*
(2. Fill config/<doctor-id>-profile.json.) Tj
T*
(3. Validate locally.) Tj
T*
(4. Test draft and preview in CMS.) Tj
T*
(5. Publish and verify live.) Tj
T*
(6. Complete go-live checklist.) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
